{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SelectiveSemiring","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:9Semirings17SelectiveSemiringP","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Semirings"}],"title":"SelectiveSemiring","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SelectiveSemiring"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/SelectiveSemiring","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A semiring whose ⊕ returns one of its operands (a selective dioid in Gondran–Minoux’s terms),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as its natural order.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/semirings\/selectivesemiring"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SL","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SQ"],"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"},{"title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BooleanSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BottleneckSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/TropicalSemiring"],"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SelectiveSemiring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Semiring","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Semirings8SemiringP","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"a < b","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly when "},{"code":"a ⊕ b == a","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"a != b","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", read as “a is better than b”. "},{"code":"a ⊕ b","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"better of the two, "},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a strict total order, and "},{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the worst element. "},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of the raw values: "},{"code":"BottleneckSemiring(9) < BottleneckSemiring(2)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because wider is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"better, and "},{"code":"BooleanSemiring(true) < BooleanSemiring(false)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra’s algorithm, Bellman–Ford, DAG shortest paths and Floyd–Warshall in ShortestPaths take"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a selective semiring. Dijkstra’s algorithm also needs every examined weight to be no better than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"one"},{"type":"text","text":", so that extending a path never improves it. A negative tropical weight breaks that, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no bottleneck or Boolean weight does."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Semirings/documentation/Semirings/TropicalSemiring":{"url":"\/documentation\/semirings\/tropicalsemiring","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The tropical semiring (min, +) over ","type":"text"},{"code":"Value","typ